 ## Capture
 
 Capture requests `echoCancellation`, `noiseSuppression`, and `autoGainControl` (mono) and logs which constraints the browser granted. AudioWorklet frames (128 samples at the device rate) go through one streaming resampler per capture session — filter state and read position carry across frames, so no sample is dropped at frame boundaries — and are sent as fixed 20 ms (640-byte) binary frames. The anti-alias filter matters for recognition: the earlier single-pole filter let 9–18 kHz content through at only 4–7 dB down, folded into 2–7 kHz; on Piper speech with added hiss above 9 kHz, Vosk word errors went from 6 % to 9–11 % with it and stayed at 6 % with the FIR. The filter costs under 1 % of one core. Microphone failures show friendly messages (denied / no device / busy) and never leave the UI parked in "Listening".
